      "content": "Traditionalist theologians primarily argue that recent secular shifts undermine the sacral nature of the family, claiming marriage is not merely a private contract but a divine institution ordained for procreation and the stable formation of virtue. They contend that redefining marriage to include same-sex unions or reducing it to emotional fulfillment erodes the objective spiritual reality necessary for meaningful moral life, which they believe was established by God regardless of social consensus. Furthermore, these critics assert that secularizing gender roles negates the anatomical and psychological complementarity essential for the differentiation of duties within marriage, ultimately leading to a fragmentation of social bonds and a loss of the shared metaphysical meaning that anchors human identity.",
